// The orphan rule over a **built-in** trait. `Clone` is part of the language, not of any package,
// so `impl Clone for <foreign type>` from a third package is an orphan exactly as a user trait's
// would be — the same judgement Rust makes about `impl std::fmt::Display for ForeignType`. Written
// in `b` (the type's own package) it would be fine.
// expect: error E0070 at 8:6
// expect: exit 1
use b.thing.{Thing};

echo Thing { id: 1 }.id
